**Known for**: NeoVim maintainer

The NeoVim website quoted an endorsement from
[David Heinemeier Hansson]($link.page('weird-guys').unsafeRef('dhh'))
until August of 2026. When an issue was opened on GitHub to complain about
using an endorsement from a fascist,[[source]][0] Justin had a bit of a crash
out, ultimately removing the quote and ending the discussion by calling those
who protested "a drive-by mob, swirling from one mindless vomit-party to
another, like the pacific garbage patch".

Justin had a YouTube playlist full of right-wing propaganda up until the DHH
debate on GitHub, including sources from [Curtis
Yarvin]($link.page('weird-guys').unsafeRef('yarvin')) and Peter Thiel. One of
Justin's co-maintainers for NeoVim, TJ DeVries, also spoke at David's Omacon in
2026.[[source]][2]

Fun fact: during the GitHub debacle over the DHH quote, Justin said "I don't
care if I end up on Drew's list", which inspired me to make this list in the
first place.

[0]: $link.url('https://github.com/neovim/neovim.github.io/issues/501').attrs('source')
[2]: $link.url('https://www.omacon.org/#speakers').attrs('source')

*Note: this page previously included a citation for Justin's YouTube playlist,
but the citation was removed after the page was purged from the Internet Archive.*
